course: dictionary
lesson: 124
title: Growing into adulthood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adulthood is the time of life when you are a grown-up. It comes after childhood and the teenage years, when your body and mind have grown and changed.
explain: «Some say 16-year-olds will live longest with today's decisions and should vote; others say 18 is the clear age of adulthood.» The people in this sentence do not agree on the age. So adulthood is not one fixed moment for everyone: people argue about when it starts.
explain: «In a baby the sutures are still open, with soft spots between the bones... they close slowly into adulthood.» Sutures are the joins between the bones of the skull. In a baby they are still open so the head can squeeze through at birth and the brain can grow. Ask: what word would fit after «close slowly into»? Growing up fits, so adulthood means the grown-up time of life.
fact: Adulthood means the time of life when you are a grown-up.
fact: Adulthood comes after childhood and the teenage years.
fact: Phrases to know: reach adulthood, in adulthood, early adulthood, into adulthood.
fact: Life goes from baby, to childhood, to adolescence (the teenage years), to adulthood.
fact: «Adulthood» is a noun, so it names a stage of life, like «childhood». We say «into adulthood», not «an adulthood».
exercise: Which two stages of life come before adulthood? | *Childhood and the teenage years | Only the first year of life | Being a baby and being a toddler | Old age and retirement
exercise: Complete the phrase: «Early ___» is the first years of being a grown-up. | kitchen | childhood | *adulthood | sunshine
exercise: «Some say 18 is the clear age of adulthood.» What does this tell you? | *People do not all agree on when adulthood starts | Everyone in the world becomes an adult on the same day | Adulthood is the same as being a baby | Adulthood means being very old
test: «The sutures close slowly into adulthood.» What does adulthood mean here? | *The grown-up time of life | A kind of bone | A short holiday | The very first day of school
test: Which word fits? «Her grandad talks about his childhood, but she is now in ___.» | *adulthood | the playground | infancy | bedtime
exam: Mia says adulthood is the same as being a teenager. Is she right? | *No, adulthood comes after the teenage years | No, adulthood is a type of bone | Yes, adulthood is the same as childhood | Yes, the teenage years and adulthood are the same time
